# Overview

- Do not use relative imports. Always use full absolute imports.
- Use css modules.
- Do not generate comments in code.
- Use css variables from `frontend/src/css/index.css` if possible and add new variables if needed.
- Use zustand for global and local client frontend state.
- Use tanstack query to store backend state.
- Use type for react props and states. Use interface only for public APIs.
- Use Recharts for creating charts.
- Use Lucide React Icons for icon.
- Use components from `frontend/src/design-system` for building features.
- Use @tanstack/react-query for data fetching at client side in the frontend.
- Use radix-ui wherever possible for components instead of creating from scratch.

# Design System

- Use the components in design-system for creating bigger components.
- Extend the design-system if the required base component is missing.
- Use Flex and Box instead of using div.
- Define CSS in the arguments of Flex and Box. Do not use CSS module files outside of the design-component. Exceptions are allowed, but this is the norm.
